From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 15:41:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 069/638] [AROS] Align desktop Autofill engagement features

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell
AI_STATUS: AROS now has a complete declaration, definition, configuration, event, and variation-registration path for the desktop Autofill IPH cohort.
ROOT_CAUSE: Desktop Autofill code references feature-engagement constants unconditionally, but AROS was omitted from every guard owning those constants and their dependent cookie-controls event.
FIX_REASON: Place AROS in the existing cross-desktop/mobile Autofill engagement cohort consistently instead of guarding individual call sites or leaving unresolved metadata.
SCOPE: Seven feature_engagement public constant/list/configuration files.
VALIDATION: Autofill suggestion generator and feature/event constant, list, and configuration objects compile; expected feature and event symbols are defined.
RISK: Low; enables existing engagement metadata on AROS, while actual presentation still depends on browser UI clients.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
